description:
The certificate checker proves an incorrect full-domain relation because every qloop-while invocation stores its private flag as the same '$loopflag' binding (checker/src/eval.rs:1530-1543).
At reviewed head 847f851cc5610ddf0edc5435c513a4ef87c6c5fc, use the valid source:
perm_action @a (t:wire mut) (c:wire in, d:wire in) () () ()
regs { } bounds {1, 1}
^entry():
qloop 1 while c {
qloop 1 while d {
x t
}
}
At (t,c,d)=(0,0,1), ISA 0.9 §4.6 requires (0,0,1); replay produces (1,0,1). A table for t'=t XOR d over all eight interface tuples returns overall=verified, claim=proof; the correct table t'=t XOR (c AND d) rejects at element 1. The inner flag overwrites the outer flag while both predicates reference the same binding.
Repro: timeout 120s cargo run --manifest-path /home/tobias/Projects/bennett-workspace/bennett-conformance/.tmp/rev-conformance/repro/Cargo.toml -j4 --quiet. Scratch fixtures nested_loop_correct and nested_loop_wrong are under .tmp/rev-conformance/. timeout 45s python3 /home/tobias/Projects/bennett-workspace/bennett-conformance/.tmp/rev-conformance/repro_gate.py independently replays the correct table as proof and rejects the wrong table. Fix round 2 must give each loop a distinct lifetime and preserve the outer predicate; cover nested inactive outer/active inner and continuation after the inner loop.
